  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open the scene in a browser, so the rendering and camera framing are untested.\n\n- **Instancing:** a 300×300 ground plane plus three instanced nodes. `trunks` (cylinders) and `canopies` (cones) have 8,000 instances each, and `rocks` (spheres) has 2,000. That is 8,000 trees and 2,000 rocks, drawn in three instanced draws.\n- **Determinism:** placement uses a seeded LCG, so the forest is the same on every load. Objects are scattered over a disc of radius 70.\n- **Colour:** canopies and rocks get per-instance HSL colours on a white base material, so the instance colours aren't applied twice.\n- **Light and fog:** one directional light with a 4096 shadow map, fitted to the forest, and exponential fog at density 0.0028. I also added a hemisphere light for fill, which is a second light but casts no shadows.\n- **Camera:** `camera.orbit` at [0, 85, 120] looking at the forest centre, with `interactions.orbit` auto-rotating at 0.08 rad/s. I chose that position so the whole forest and ground fit in frame, but I haven't checked it by eye.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after the first `onFrame` callback.\n\nThe shadow fit (`extent: 85`) is my guess at how the engine reads that option, so check that shadows cover the whole forest.\n\n",
